Well. In third-world countries (like Iran) where people pay only 4 
dollars to get Visual Studio 2010, and 99% of the population can't 
google, I don't think that would increase my chance for a job. :-)

I end up using PHP for two years and when looking for a job, I am told 
that I do not know anything about web development because, well, surely, 
web developing = using ASP.net, right? :)

With Visual Web Developer Express working, though, I think i'm in better 
luck, thanks to Jamal and other people on this list again! (my computer 
is filled up with the programs/scripts Jamal's written!)

Take care.

